  "_comment": "Shared cross-module golden for the specialist-job wire contract (E85.9 / #4300). job is a GET /v0/specialist-jobs/{job_id} body (server specialistJobResponse -> runner upload.SpecialistJob; never execution_nonce). admission is a POST .../admission answer. admission_attested is the same answer as an attester's admission delivers it (E85.15 / #4363): attestation_key is the base64 std encoding of the 64-byte Ed25519 private key derived from result_attestation.seed_hex. result_attestation is the byte-exact result-signature vector: message_hex = sha256(\"fishhawk-specialist-job-result-v1\\u0000\" || job_id || 0x00 || sha256(body)) and signature_hex = Ed25519(seed, message) (deterministic, RFC 8032); the backend specialistjob.ResultMessage and the runner upload.SpecialistJobResultMessage both recompute it. completions holds one valid POST .../result body per runner-executed kind plus an inconclusive-with-reason one (runner upload.SpecialistJobCompletion -> specialistjob.Completion). Backend tests ParseCompletion every entry; runner tests round-trip every entry through the upload structs with DisallowUnknownFields.",
